---
description: >-
  Every block label kind, each written five ways (D734, D736): shapes in the
  first row, block arrows in the second, composites in the third and edge
  labels between the last two rows. Columns, left to right: markdown markers
  in a plain label (drawn as written), a markdown string (bold and italic), a
  code span in a plain label (drawn as written), the drawn tags, and a written
  backslash-n (two lines). A label in bare backticks is not quoted, which the
  grammar rejects as v12 did, so it is left out.
---
block
  columns 5
  s1["shape **bold** _ital_"]
  s2["`shape **bold** _ital_`"]
  s3["shape a `code` b"]
  s4["shape <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"]
  s5["shape one\ntwo"]
  r1<["arrow **bold** _ital_"]>(right)
  r2<["`arrow **bold** _ital_`"]>(right)
  r3<["arrow a `code` b"]>(right)
  r4<["arrow <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"]>(right)
  r5<["arrow one\ntwo"]>(right)
  block:g1["group **bold** _ital_"]
    i1
  end
  block:g2["`group **bold** _ital_`"]
    i2
  end
  block:g3["group a `code` b"]
    i3
  end
  block:g4["group <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"]
    i4
  end
  block:g5["group one\ntwo"]
    i5
  end
  e1 e2 e3 e4 e5
  space:5
  f1 f2 f3 f4 f5
  e1 -- "edge **bold** _ital_" --> f1
  e2 -- "`edge **bold** _ital_`" --> f2
  e3 -- "edge a `code` b" --> f3
  e4 -- "edge <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O" --> f4
  e5 -- "edge one\ntwo" --> f5
